      "value": "@{6075548fb0c5603e04a7fe69|full_name} This is true; the workaround I've used in the past with FinalIK is to instead target the UI Layer (Player Capsule) on the local client, and translate the hit distance via contacts, to mixed success.\n\nBut in the video, despite using the 'Custom Layers - Everything' tag, it wasn't colliding with the UI Layer either..\n\nGranted I realize the goal of the VRCRaycast Component isn't to replicate FinalIK's function 1-to-1, but it would be nice to have some way to reasonably view collisions with remote players c.c",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
