      "value": "@{612a02ff537735196f11ff83|full_name} You shouldn't be relying on the UI Layer (And UIMenu). Pretty sure those only exist when your menu is open in some capacity (at least that's how it is for UIMenu). Tho I've yet to try that myself. The only \"consistent\" collider on remote players is the Player collider but because it differs in size, shape and position you can't realistically do much with it outside of offsetting your objects locally to match or attach an object to the player with the funky contact tracker tech-",
